WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:01.726
Addition combines quantities

00:00:01.726 --> 00:00:05.703
Start with six dots and bring in four more

00:00:05.703 --> 00:00:14.100
Counting the joined collection gives ten, while keeping the original groups visible shows exactly which two amounts were combined.

00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:17.429
Subtraction can undo that combination

00:00:17.429 --> 00:00:20.676
Removing the four newly added dots leaves six

00:00:20.676 --> 00:00:29.200
We can also ask for the missing addend: what must join four to make ten? Both questions identify the same quantity.

00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:33.925
For larger numbers, break one amount into convenient parts

00:00:33.925 --> 00:00:41.156
To add twenty five to thirty eight, add twenty to reach fifty eight, then five to reach sixty three

00:00:41.156 --> 00:00:44.200
We changed the steps, not the total increase.

00:00:45.500 --> 00:00:48.722
Reverse those same moves to check the result

00:00:48.722 --> 00:00:53.556
Subtract five and then twenty from sixty three, returning to thirty eight

00:00:53.556 --> 00:01:00.000
A sensible subtraction answer must rebuild the original total when the removed amount is added back.
